item linux-io-native.bot seconds 1.647 status 0 cpu {1.587 0.048} result {backends {interp {excluded {CORE SEMANTIC NATIVE-ONLY: linux::abi::syscall executes the x86-64 syscall instruction and the Tcl backends refuse it at run time by design (tests/linux-syscall.test linux-syscall-tcl-backends-refuse pins the refusal); a refusal aborts a suite, so these tests run on cranelift-generic and cranelift only}}}}
item abi-bytes-native.bot seconds 1.796 status 0 cpu {1.757 0.028} result {backends {interp {excluded {CORE SEMANTIC NATIVE-ONLY: linux::write takes its payload's machine address (abi::x86_64::from_bytes) for the write(2) syscall, which the Tcl backends refuse at run time by design (tests/abi-bytes.test abi-bytes-tcl-backends-refuse-the-address pins the refusal); a refusal aborts a suite, so these tests run on cranelift-generic and cranelift only}}}}
